title: OS/arch/build defines are all on at once (MANIA64+MANIA32, WINDOWS+LINUX+WINDOWS_WINE)
updated_at: "2026-08-29T08:57:53Z"
---
Found 2026-08-29 while implementing GH #64 (signature-mode selector). Same
class as GH #36 (platform selectors) and GH #64 (signature levels): a set of
mutually-exclusive-in-reality defines is switched on simultaneously.

## What is wrong
`LspConfig::defines_for_target` ALWAYS_ON currently holds:

    MANIA64, MANIA32, WINDOWS, WINDOWS_WINE, LINUX, SERVER, LOGS, HAS_DEV, DEVELOPER

No real Openplanet process has more than one of {MANIA64, MANIA32} or of
{WINDOWS, LINUX} live, and WINDOWS_WINE only under Wine. Per the docs
(https://openplanet.dev/docs/reference/preprocessor) the rest describe the
running build: DEVELOPER = "the current Openplanet build is a debug build",
HAS_DEV = "the current game is a Nadeo development build", LOGS = "a
Logs-configured build", SERVER = "a dedicated server build" — a normal
player's client has none of the last three.

## Impact
A plugin that declares the same symbol in separate `#if MANIA32` and
`#if MANIA64` blocks (or `#if WINDOWS` / `#if LINUX`) gets BOTH branches
analyzed, so the second declaration is a phantom duplicate-declaration error.
Code inside `#if SERVER` — never compiled on a client — is analyzed too, and
its diagnostics are noise for a plugin that only ships to clients.

Lower frequency than GH #36/#64 (fewer plugins branch on arch/OS), which is
why it is filed rather than folded into #64.

## Sketch
Follow the shape GH #64 landed for signatures — selector keys, not hand-listed
defines, resolved through the same ladder and derived in `defines_for_target`:

- `os_target = "windows" | "linux" | "wine"` (default windows; wine implies
  WINDOWS + WINDOWS_WINE, matching the game).
- `arch_target = "64" | "32"` (default 64).
- Build flags as booleans with client defaults: `developer_build`,
  `has_dev`, `logs`, `server` — all default FALSE except keeping today's
  behavior in mind (see migration).
- CLI `--os` / `--arch` alongside `--game-target` / `--signature`.

## Migration hazard (decide before implementing)
Unlike GH #64 — where the always-on set WAS the developer level, so the
default changed nothing — turning these off changes the default analysis for
everyone: code inside `#if SERVER` / `#if LOGS` / `#if HAS_DEV` / one of the
arch branches stops being checked, and symbols declared only there become
undefined at their use sites. Options: (a) default them all ON (status quo)
and let users narrow — safe but leaves the duplicate-declaration bug on by
default; (b) default to a realistic client profile and take the churn in a
minor release with a loud CHANGELOG entry. Recommend (a) for the flags plus a
real default for os/arch (windows + 64), since arch/OS duplicates are the
actual reported failure mode. Needs a decision, not just an implementation.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Red: a fixture declaring `int x;` in both `#if MANIA32` and `#if MANIA64`
must report 0 diagnostics (today: duplicate declaration). Variants: WINDOWS vs
LINUX pair; `os_target = "wine"` defines WINDOWS and WINDOWS_WINE together;
`#if SERVER` code is not analyzed under a client profile; `defines` overrides
still get the last word (`defines = ["SERVER"]` re-enables it); CLI flags beat
config; unknown values are a usage error / warn-and-keep like #64.

Decision (2026-08-29, coordinator): adopt the ticket's option (a) — developer_build/has_dev/logs/server default ON (no default churn); os_target (windows|linux|wine, default windows; wine => WINDOWS + WINDOWS_WINE) and arch_target (64|32, default 64) get realistic defaults since the OS/arch duplicate-declaration is the reported failure mode. Operator note (Max): verify the wine define set EMPIRICALLY with a spite probe plugin before baking it in — expected WINDOWS + WINDOWS_WINE (and NOT LINUX); probe arch + SERVER/LOGS/HAS_DEV/DEVELOPER the same way while at it. Parallel lane with B023/B027 (disjoint src files: config.rs/cli/preprocessor vs checker.rs); shared append-only files (fixture README, cli_check_tests.rs) merge last. Ops: wrap EVERY game probe in: flock /tmp/lsp-openplanet-game-probe.lock -c '<cmd>'.

Resolved (2026-08-29). Empirical define set verified via spite probes in the live game under Wine (fixtures b028-os-arch-defines-probe, b028-build-flag-probe): WINDOWS + WINDOWS_WINE + MANIA64 ON; LINUX/MANIA32/SERVER/LOGS/HAS_DEV/DEVELOPER OFF. Implemented per decision (a): OsTarget/ArchTarget/BuildFlags selector enums through the GH #64 ladder; CLI --os/--arch; B024 overrides keep last word. Merged to master d548b98 (branch fix/b028-os-arch-defines, commits 3914d23 + 05d45b5). Independent reviewer: APPROVE. Deliberate omissions: TUI/user-config SETTINGS catalog rows for the six new keys (reviewer nit — signature_mode is already missing there too; hand-written configs + CLI fully work); reviewer finding 5 retracted (--os/--arch swallow-guard rows exist). Test gate: full cargo test green on master post-merge.